What the two legs measured
--------------------------
Leg 1 birthright_entry, the REAL shipped pay product: price 19.90, entitlement
"birthright", activation accepted with tier=null, permanent=true, period count 0,
privilege count 0. So the first-yuan product delivers a permanent birth
certificate and no membership tier, no credits and no privileges.

Leg 2 tier_experience, a dock row that exists ONLY in the temp copy of the pay
config (a real monthly price row is a needs-CEO approval face): price 19.90 as
well, entitlement "tier:experience", activation accepted with tier=experience,
period count 1, period length 30 days, credits 3, privileges
basic_badge + emoji_pack_standard, and the privilege set EQUALS the member
catalog declaration for that tier.

That is the finding: two products at the identical 19.90 price deliver wildly
different value, and the one that is actually shipped is the one with the
smaller value. The page states the difference rather than showing two tables.

